<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
    <!--
        The app is intentionally NOT sandboxed.

        Browsing siblings of the opened image requires reading the parent
        directory. Under App Sandbox, `com.apple.security.files.user-selected.*`
        only grants access to the file the user explicitly picked through
        Powerbox, not to its parent folder, so `FileManager.contentsOfDirectory`
        silently fails and arrow-key navigation does nothing.

        macOS still applies TCC (per-folder consent prompts for Desktop /
        Documents / Downloads / iCloud Drive / etc.) on first access, which is
        the right level of protection for a local image viewer.
    -->
</dict>
</plist>
